            <ArticleTitle>Can computers improve the Health of the Nation?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>889-93</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this paper the author considers whether the use of computers can be demonstrated to have a positive impact upon the effectiveness of health screening, in accordance with the Health of the Nation document. It is based upon a study of 1.1 million patients registered with 283 general practices in the North West region of the UK.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
